The files under `not_wf/` and `wf/` are test cases of the W3C XML Conformance Test Suite, release
20130923 (https://www.w3.org/XML/Test/xmlts20130923.tar.gz), which the W3C distributes under the
W3C Software Notice and License below (https://www.w3.org/XML/Test/XMLConformanceTS-Process-20031210.html,
section 6).

Changes made here, 2026-10-05: the cases the suite's catalogs list for XML 1.0 Fifth Edition were
selected and copied, each byte for byte, to `not_wf/` and `wf/` under the path it has in the suite.
No file was altered. Left out are the catalogs, the external entities and declarations the cases
refer to, the suite's own output files, the cases for XML 1.1 and for editions before the fifth, and
every file of James Clark's `xmltest` collection, which its notice lets be passed on only whole: the
cases under `xmltest/`, and `eduni/errata-4e/140.xml` and `141.xml`, which are two of them again.

The files under `canonical/` are not the suite's: each was made for this repository, on the same
day, from what the expat parser reads of the case of the same path under `wf/`, written in the first
canonical form the suite's documentation defines.

The suite carries these notices of its contributors, each over the directory named:

  sun/: Copyright 1998 by Sun Microsystems, Inc. All Rights Reserved.

  oasis/: no notice of its own.

  japanese/: its catalog, Copyright 1998 by Sun Microsystems, Inc. All Rights Reserved; the
  declarations its `weekly` cases refer to, Copyright 1997 Fuji Xerox Information Systems Co.,Ltd.
  Its `pr-xml` cases are a translation into Japanese of the XML proposed recommendation of December
  1997, and give that document's notice: "This version of the XML specification is for public review
  and discussion. It may be distributed freely, as long as all text and legal notices remain intact."

  ibm/: (C) Copyright IBM Corp. 2000 All rights reserved. US Government Users Restricted Rights Use,
